To create a dynamic webpage that changes the appearance of the sun based on the time of day using PHP and CSS, you would need to:
1. Use PHP to get the current date and time.
2. Determine whether it is daytime or nighttime based on the current time.
3. Use CSS to style the sun image accordingly.
Here's some sample code to get you started:
```php
<?php
$current_time = time();
$daylight_savings_offset = 0; // adjust for daylight savings time if necessary

// determine whether it is daytime or nighttime
$is_daytime = $current_time > ($daylight_savings_offset + (6 * 60 * 60)) && $current_time < ($daylight_savings_offset + (18 * 60 * 60));

// set up variables for the sun image
$sun_image_url = 'sun.png';
if ($is_daytime) {
    $sun_image_url .= '?daytime=true'; 
} else {
    $sun_image_url .= '?nighttime=true';
}
?>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Sun Appearance</title>
    <style>
        .sun {
            width: 100px;
            height: 100px;
            background-image: url('<?php echo $sun_image_url; ?>');
            background-size: cover;
            position: absolute;
            top: 50%;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="sun"></div>
</body>
</html>
```
